 ## shell.css
 
-### §container-not-viewport — the shell responds to its own width
+### §viewport-not-container — the shell's layout steps use viewport media queries
+- Since: 2026-10-22
+- Supersedes: §container-not-viewport
+- Decision: the shell's layout steps use viewport `@media` width queries (`min-width: 720px`). `.shell` no longer
+  sets `container-type`.
+- Reason: agreed in the team sync on 2026-10-22 to drop container queries because much of the team has not used
+  them.
+- Known trade-off: the shell still renders inside split panes. A narrow pane on a wide screen gets the two-column
+  layout again, which is the failure behind the 2026-09-14 incident below.
+
+### §container-not-viewport — the shell responds to its own width (superseded 2026-10-22 by §viewport-not-container)
 - Since: 2026-09-15
 - Decision: the shell's layout steps use `@container` queries on `.shell`.
 - Forbidden: switching the shell's layout steps to viewport `@media` width queries (`min-width` / `max-width`).
